  "authoringNote": "Migrated from F22; expectations re-derived under pack v2. The worksheet f22-worksheet v1 is a supporting note bound to the case subject (metadata, stated name and identifier exact), so R02 passes and cites its name and identifier with those of the encounter, order and receipt (eight). No rule reads note text, and R07 imposes no ATP, specialty evaluation, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item on an initial K0823 packet, so the worksheet's \"not on file\" statements create no condition. Encounter 2026-08-18 and order 2026-08-31 are final with the same practitioner identifier and sequenced; the receipt at 2026-09-01 follows the order span. All administrative rules pass with ordinary citations, R06 and R10 as always, and the state is ready_for_review, as in v1.",
